---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { email, address, legalName, tdiLicense } from "../site.js";
---

<Base
  title="Licensing & Disclosures — Stonework Risk"
  description="Licensing, compensation and consumer information for Stonework Risk, an independent insurance agency in Dallas, Texas."
  path="/licensing"
>
  <main class="doc">
    <h1>Licensing &amp; Disclosures</h1>
    <p class="updated">Stonework Risk · Dallas, Texas</p>

    <h2>Licensing</h2>
    <p>
      Stonework Risk is the assumed name of {legalName}, an independent insurance agency
      licensed by the Texas Department of Insurance{tdiLicense && <> (agency license no. {tdiLicense})</>}.
      Our office is at {address.street}, {address.city}, {address.state} {address.zip}.
    </p>
    <p>
      Insurance is placed only in states where the agency and its producers hold the
      required licenses. License status can be verified with the
      <a href="https://www.tdi.texas.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Texas Department of Insurance</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How we are paid</h2>
    <p>
      Like most independent agencies, we are typically paid a commission by the insurance
      company that issues your policy, calculated as a percentage of the premium. Some
      carriers also pay agencies additional compensation based on the overall volume,
      growth or profitability of the business placed with them. Where a service fee
      applies, it will be disclosed to you in writing before you agree to it.
    </p>
    <p>
      You are welcome to ask about the compensation we receive on any policy we place for
      you, and we'll tell you.
    </p>

    <h2>Not a guarantee of coverage</h2>
    <p>
      Information on this website is general in nature and does not describe or modify
      any insurance policy. Coverage is subject to underwriting review and to the terms,
      conditions and exclusions of the policy actually issued. Coverage is not bound
      until confirmed in writing by Stonework Risk or the issuing carrier. Submitting the
      contact form does not bind, change or cancel coverage.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions or complaints</h2>
    <p>
      If you have a question or concern about our service, contact us first at
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> — we'd like the chance to make it right.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also contact the Texas Department of Insurance for information on
      companies, coverages, rights or complaints:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Consumer Help Line: 1-800-252-3439</li>
      <li>Online: <a href="https://www.tdi.texas.gov" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.tdi.texas.gov</a></li>
    </ul>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to stoneworkrisk.com</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
